  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Egypt - Support to Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises in Organic Clusters Project</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Egypte - Projet de soutien aux micro, petites et moyennes entreprises dans les clusters biologiques</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Le projet d&apos;appui aux Micro, Petites et Moyennes Entreprises (MPME) dans les groupes organiques s&apos;inscrit dans le cadre de la politique globale des MPME en cours de d&#xe9;veloppement et dirig&#xe9; par le Fonds social pour le d&#xe9;veloppement (SFD). Le projet comprend trois (03) composantes, &#xe0; savoir: A) les recommandations politiques visant &#xe0; cr&#xe9;er un environnement propice au d&#xe9;veloppement des MPME dans les grappes organiques; B) le renforcement des capacit&#xe9;s institutionnelles et op&#xe9;rationnelles pour les principales institutions de soutien et les parties prenantes travaillant avec des groupes organiques de MPME; C) l&apos;augmentation de la contribution organique des MPME &#xe0; la valeur ajout&#xe9;e manufacturi&#xe8;re (projet pilote).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MSMEs are important drivers for poverty reduction and job creation, as they represent over 99.7% of all private non-agricultural enterprises in Egypt, account for 85% of non-agricultural private sector employment, and almost 40% of total employment. MSMEs have been the primary absorber of labor force entrants over the past years and contribute significantly to employment generation, albeit mostly in the informal sector. MSMEs are also the major provider of products and services for local markets, particularly for lower-income segments with limited purchasing power. It is widely believed that the MSMEs and the informal sector at large have acted as a solid buffer, attenuating the impact of the crisis on Egyptians, particularly the vulnerable groups. Despite its potential, the MSME sector faces a multiplicity of constraints that hinder its performance and affects the outcome of its role as an economic catalyst. In addition to the well-known financial constraints, MSMEs face a myriad of non-financial obstacles such as obtaining the required inputs, producing and marketing a competitive product, obtaining knowledge on the latest know-how and on market requirements, in addition to an inadequate institutional, legal and regulatory environment.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Les principaux b&#xe9;n&#xe9;ficiaires du projet sont: le Gouvernement de la R&#xe9;publique Arabe d&apos;&#xc9;gypte, le Fonds Social pour le D&#xe9;veloppement (SFD), les Micro, Petites et Moyennes Entreprises (MPME).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main beneficiaries of the project are: The Government of the Arab Republic of Egypt, the Social Fund for Development (SFD), the Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Les principaux objectifs de ce projet sont les suivants: cr&#xe9;er un environnement favorable g&#xe9;n&#xe9;ral pour les Micro, Petites et Moyennes Entreprises (MPME) op&#xe9;rant &#xe0; partir de grappes organiques et accro&#xee;tre leur contribution &#xe0; la croissance &#xe9;conomique et &#xe0; l&apos;emploi.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The principal objectives of this project are to: create an overall enabling environment for Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) operating out of organic clusters and increase their contribution towards economic growth and employment.</narrative>
  </description>
